    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200254409679_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Bus Driver",
      "description": "Posted: 2022-02-02\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nHuntington University seeks part-time bus drivers for a 35 passenger bus.  The Bus Driver is responsible for transporting students, staff, coaches, and passengers safely to and from their destination in the established times and in all types of weather and road conditions, observing legal, safe, and defensive driving practices.  QUALIFICATIONS:   Must have a strong personal faith in Jesus Christ, a desire to serve others and a commitment to being a faithful steward of university resources Must have a “clean” driving record Have sufficient physical and mental abilities to operate a school bus/van in a safe manner Must be narcotic drug and alcohol free Professional driving experience preferred This is a part-time, on call position Must possess a valid commercial driver’s with passenger endorsement Minimum age of 25 years  RESPONSIBILITIES:   Bus/Van Maintain vehicle by conducting safety inspection, inspect the interior and exterior and the engine prior to use Maintain order among passengers and report any behavioral issues to the appropriate personnel, assure passengers understand bus rules of safety Assist students, staff, coaches, and passengers in and out of vehicle as needed Assist students, staff, coaches, and passengers with loading and unloading equipment as needed   Administrative   Collaborate with coaching and administrative staff to establish transportation schedule Maintain and update route sheets and schedules, manifesto along with emergency contact information Assist with other projects and perform other duties as assigned by the VP of Business & Finance Treasurer  Physical Requirements of the Position:   Employee is regularly required to focus, see, speak, and hear and to have dexterity of the hands and fingers Must be able to sit for extended periods of time while driving Other duties may require bending, kneeling, twisting, and reaching overhead, above shoulders and horizontally May be required to lift, carry, and/or push moderately heavy persons in effort to evacuate the bus/van in case of emergency Shall be required to meet all regulatory standards as directed by the State of Indiana as a driver General Information:   Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university.  Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals.   Statement of Faith Work Schedule:  This is a part-time, non-exempt position.  The driving schedule varies depending on scheduling and workflow demands. To Apply: Review the full job description attached for a complete list of responsibilities and qualifications. Apply via ADP, using your personal email, and upload a cover letter, resume and list of references with your completed application. Questions can be emailed to Andy McKee, Director of Human Resources.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205222645102_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "OTA Lab and Administrative Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-10\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nHuntington University has an opening for a OTA Lab and Administrative Coordinator. The OTA Lab and Administrative Coordinator supports the daily operation of the Occupational Therapy Assistant program by maintaining the OTA classroom and laboratory environments and providing administrative support to faculty, students, and program leadership. QUALIFICATIONS Strong personal faith in Jesus Christ and an understanding of the relationship between faith and professional practice. Occupational Therapy Assistant (OTA) certification preferred. Candidates with relevant patient care experience in a health-related field, such as experience as a Certified Nursing Assistant (CNA), Patient Care Technician (PCT), rehabilitation aide, or similar role, will also be considered. Commitment to supporting an occupational therapy practice curriculum grounded in the mission of the University and reflective of Christian ethics, compassion, and service. Strong organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills, with the ability to work collaboratively with faculty, students, the University community, and clinical partners. Proficiency with computer applications and technology needed to support departmental operations. Demonstrated commitment to stewardship and service to others. Commitment to maintaining confidentiality and handling sensitive information with professionalism and discretion. Self-directed, innovative, and able to assess current operations, identify areas for improvement, and develop practical strategies to enhance departmental functioning.   General Information:   Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts University.  Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals.   Statement of Faith Work Schedule:  This is a part time, non-exempt, 9-month position, working 20 hours per week.  To Apply: Review the full job description attached for a complete list of responsibilities and qualifications. Apply via ADP, using your personal email, and upload a cover letter, resume and list of references with your completed application. Questions can be emailed to Andy McKee, Director of Human Resources.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205230681607_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach Track & Field- Throws",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nHuntington University has an opening for an Assistant Coach for Track & Field-Throws. The Track & Field Assistant Coach for Throws is a part-time position that supports the overall mission of the Track & Field program by providing expert technical instruction and mentorship to student-athletes in the throwing events. Grounded in Christ-centered values and a commitment to the University's mission, this role helps foster a caring, faith-driven environment where athletes are developed spiritually, personally, and competitively.  Responsibilities include coaching, recruiting, and administrative tasks as assigned by the head coach ensuring all operations reflect compliance with NAIA, conference, and institutional regulations.  QUALIFICATIONS Christ-centered Faithfulness: A deep personal commitment to Jesus Christ and a passion for the mission of Huntington University, dedicated to mentoring student-athletes to impact the world for Christ. Commitment to Excellence: Proven skills in coaching, administration, and leadership Creativity and Innovation:  Demonstration of forward-thinking approaches to skill development, team-building, problem-solving, and continuous process improvement. Collaborative Spirit: Evidence of ability to effectively communicate and collaborate with Athletic department personnel and to achieve shared team, department, and institutional goals. Community Conviction: Exceptional interpersonal skills, with the ability to build a supportive and growth-oriented culture for student-athletes and staff. GENERAL RESPONSIBILITIES: Coaching Serve as a consistent Christian role model, intentionally developing and mentoring student-athletes to grow in their faith and to impact our world for Christ. Plan and organize practices for the jumps events to maximize student-athlete potential and program performance. Recruiting Aid head coach in identifying and recruiting student-athletes who align with the HU mission, prioritizing those who are a strong fit for the university's spiritual, academic, and athletic standards. Develop an understanding of NAIA recruiting policies in order to maintain a high level of integrity throughout the recruiting process. Administrative Duties Maintain high standards of excellence and timeliness in completing administrative tasks assigned by the head coach. Proactively anticipate program needs to enhance the student-athlete experience and work with the head coach to create a plan to meet the needs. Collaboration & Supervision Foster a collaborative spirit by working closely with the head coach and other coaching staff to ensure effective program operations. Communicate and enforce team rules that promote a culture of accountability and care. Comply with all NAIA, Crossroads League, and institutional policies. General Information:   Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university.  Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals.   Statement of Faith Work Schedule:  This is a part-time position.   To Apply: Review the full job description attached for a complete list of responsibilities and qualifications. Apply via ADP, using your personal email, and upload a cover letter, resume and list of references with your completed application. Questions can be emailed to Andy McKee, Director of Human Resources.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205230679911_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach Track & Field - Jumps",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nHuntington University has an opening for an Assistant Coach for Track & Field-Jumps The Track & Field Assistant Coach for Jumps is a part-time position that supports the overall mission of the Track & Field program by providing expert technical instruction and mentorship to student-athletes in the jumping events. Grounded in Christ-centered values and a commitment to the University's mission, this role helps foster a caring, faith-driven environment where athletes are developed spiritually, personally, and competitively.  Responsibilities include coaching, recruiting, and administrative tasks as assigned by the head coach ensuring all operations reflect compliance with NAIA, conference, and institutional regulations.  QUALIFICATIONS Christ-centered Faithfulness: A deep personal commitment to Jesus Christ and a passion for the mission of Huntington University, dedicated to mentoring student-athletes to impact the world for Christ. Commitment to Excellence: Proven skills in coaching, administration, and leadership Creativity and Innovation:  Demonstration of forward-thinking approaches to skill development, team-building, problem-solving, and continuous process improvement. Collaborative Spirit: Evidence of ability to effectively communicate and collaborate with Athletic department personnel and to achieve shared team, department, and institutional goals. Community Conviction: Exceptional interpersonal skills, with the ability to build a supportive and growth-oriented culture for student-athletes and staff. GENERAL RESPONSIBILITIES: Coaching Serve as a consistent Christian role model, intentionally developing and mentoring student-athletes to grow in their faith and to impact our world for Christ. Plan and organize practices for the jumps events to maximize student-athlete potential and program performance. Recruiting Aid head coach in identifying and recruiting student-athletes who align with the HU mission, prioritizing those who are a strong fit for the university's spiritual, academic, and athletic standards. Develop an understanding of NAIA recruiting policies in order to maintain a high level of integrity throughout the recruiting process. Administrative Duties Maintain high standards of excellence and timeliness in completing administrative tasks assigned by the head coach. Proactively anticipate program needs to enhance the student-athlete experience and work with the head coach to create a plan to meet the needs. Collaboration & Supervision Foster a collaborative spirit by working closely with the head coach and other coaching staff to ensure effective program operations. Communicate and enforce team rules that promote a culture of accountability and care. Comply with all NAIA, Crossroads League, and institutional policies. General Information:   Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university.  Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals.   Statement of Faith Work Schedule:  This is a part-time position.   To Apply: Review the full job description attached for a complete list of responsibilities and qualifications. Apply via ADP, using your personal email, and upload a cover letter, resume and list of references with your completed application. Questions can be emailed to Andy McKee, Director of Human Resources.",
